USOS CSMWrap patch 0018 (2026-10-18): USB mouse wheel diagnostics record

Windows Me on the X470 (CSMWrap 3.1.2-usos13): the USB mouse moves and
clicks, the wheel does nothing. Patch 0016 decides at setup between the HID
report protocol (wheel) and the boot protocol; nothing showed which one it
took and why. With this patch SeaBIOS keeps a small record in its low
memory zone (VARLOW, 16-byte aligned, signature "USOS" "MWHL" written at
setup, version 1), read by USOSDBG.EXE from the first MiB:
- per mouse (first 4): interface number, wMaxPacketSize, report or boot
  protocol, a reason code when boot (long item, bad report ID, nested Push,
  Pop without Push, too many report IDs, field too big, a report longer
  than one packet, no relative X / Y / wheel / button 1, X without report
  ID, no HID descriptor, descriptor too long, no memory, GET_DESCRIPTOR or
  SET_PROTOCOL failed), report ID, wDescriptorLength, the parsed layout;
- the first 160 bytes of the first mouse's report descriptor;
- the IntelliMouse state (device ID, last two sample rates), the number of
  packets, of packets with a nonzero wheel value and of skipped packets of
  other report IDs, the last raw packet and its wheel value.
hid_parse_mouse returns these reason codes instead of -1; every decision is
the same as in 0016 (0 = report protocol, any negative value = boot). The
record is only written, never read by the BIOS; the keyboard path, the PS/2
BIOS INT 15h C2xxh behaviour and the packets passed on are unchanged.

Own code. Applies after 0001-0010, 0012, 0014-0017, patch -p1 from the top
of the tree. Part of a MODIFIED CSMWrap made by the USOS project (SeaBIOS
LGPLv3).

diff -ruN a/seabios/src/hw/usb-hid.c b/seabios/src/hw/usb-hid.c
--- a/seabios/src/hw/usb-hid.c
+++ b/seabios/src/hw/usb-hid.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
